From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:06:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 178/269] gallium: drop the native pvr driver's build entries;
 wrapper takes the pvr slot

The Imagination PVR Gallium frontend (mesa-pvr-vf2, built as a standalone Mesa 22.1.7 at
/home/radxa/mesa-pvr) owns the 'pvr' driver name and dri/pvr_dri.so. The native driver's code moved to
drivers/pvr_native keeping its history; these are the leftover registration edits from that move.

Native driver work is preserved at drivers/pvr_native and in git history; reviving it needs one meson
entry. It remains incomplete - no draw path.
---
 src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.h b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.h
index a9dd5101..aff629f0 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.h
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.h
@@ -191,6 +191,8 @@ extern const struct __DriverAPIRec galliumvk_driver_api;
 extern const __DRIextension *galliumvk_driver_extensions[];
 extern const __DRIconfigOptionsExtension gallium_config_options;
 
+extern const struct __DriverAPIRec pvr_driver_api;
+extern const __DRIextension *pvr_driver_extensions[];
 #endif
 
 /* vim: set sw=3 ts=8 sts=3 expandtab: */
